    text: "@boundary_method: mechanical_word_chunk"
  - line: 5
    type: narration
    text: "@authority_state: SCENE_BOUNDARY_MECHANICAL"
  - line: 6
    type: narration
    text: "@authored_scene_boundaries_proven: false"
  - line: 7
    type: narration
    text: "@boundary_start_line: 56"
  - line: 8
    type: narration
    text: "@boundary_end_line: 131"
  - line: 9
    type: narration
    text: "@contract: engain.scene_text_packet.v1"
  - line: 10
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 11
    type: narration
    text: "They reached the plateau by midday."
  - line: 12
    type: narration
    text: "The air was thinner here, cooler."
  - line: 13
    type: narration
    text: "The place was unremarkable—just a flat stretch of wind-scoured stone between two ridges—but both Geralt and Mika stopped as if struck."
  - line: 15
    type: narration
    text: "Mika walked to a particular depression in the rock, her boots scuffing the stone."
  - line: 16
    type: narration
    text: "\"I fell here,\" she said, her voice quiet."
  - line: 17
    type: narration
    text: "\"I was following your blood."
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "I thought it was leading me to you."
  - line: 19
    type: narration
    text: "I collapsed right here.\""
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt moved a few meters to the east, to a patch of darker stone."
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "\"I fell here first."
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "Before you ever came looking."
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "The Nexus spat me out."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "I crawled this far before I passed out.\""
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "They stood in silence, the space between them suddenly charged with the ghost of those terrible, lonely hours."
  - line: 28
    type: narration
    text: "They had been meters apart, each unconscious, each believing the other was lost forever."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "The distance felt vast and insignificant all at once."
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "Then, a cry from above."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "Three falcons circled against the hard blue sky."
  - line: 34
    type: narration
    text: "They were the same ones—Mika knew it in her gut."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "They wheeled once, twice, then dove sharply beyond the northern rise."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "Mika and Geralt looked at each other."
  - line: 39
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Again?\""
  - line: 41
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"Again,\""
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "They followed, their small company trailing behind."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "They crested the rise—"
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "—and the valley opened below them."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "It was hidden, perfectly sheltered by the surrounding ridges."
  - line: 49
    type: narration
    text: "A clear stream cut through its center, fed by a waterfall that cascaded from the eastern cliff."
  - line: 50
    type: narration
    text: "Ancient, gnarled trees dotted the slopes, and the floor was rich, dark soil."
  - line: 51
    type: narration
    text: "It was a bowl of life carved into the stone desert."
  - line: 53
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"The place we missed by fifty meters,\""
  - line: 55
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt pointed."
  - line: 56
    type: narration
    text: "High on the cliff face, beneath the falcons' now-visible nest, a scrap of fabric fluttered."
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "Mika scrambled up the loose scree, her heart pounding."
  - line: 58
    type: narration
    text: "She pulled it free."
  - line: 60
    type: narration
    text: "It was the scarf."
  - line: 61
    type: narration
    text: "Her scarf."
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "The one she'd lost years ago on this very plateau, the one with the ambiguous, blood-stained pattern that could be a falcon or a dragon."
  - line: 63
    type: narration
    text: "It was sun-faded, but the stain was still there."
  - line: 64
    type: narration
    text: "His blood."
  - line: 65
    type: narration
    text: "Her history."
  - line: 67
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"How is this here?\""
  - line: 69
    type: narration
    text: "No answer came."
  - line: 70
    type: narration
    text: "The wind sighed through the valley."
  - line: 71
    type: narration
    text: "Some rhymes in reality had no reason, only resonance."
  - line: 73
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt climbed up to join her."
  - line: 74
    type: narration
    text: "He took the scarf from her trembling hands."
  - line: 75
    type: narration
    text: "He found a straight, strong branch from a fallen tree."
  - line: 76
    type: narration
    text: "With careful, deliberate movements, he tied the scarf to one end."
  - line: 77
    type: narration
    text: "He carried it down into the heart of the valley, to where the stream entered from the north."
  - line: 78
    type: narration
    text: "He drove the branch deep into the earth."
  - line: 80
    type: narration
    text: "The makeshift banner caught the breeze, the faded fabric snapping once, then settling."
  - line: 82
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"Welcome to Falcon Ridge,\""
  - line: 84
    type: narration
    text: "And they began to build."
  - line: 86
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 3: EARLY DAYS"
  - line: 88
    type: narration
    text: "Month 1 was raw survival."
  - line: 89
    type: narration
    text: "They cleared a flat space near the stream with axes and sheer will."
  - line: 90
    type: narration
    text: "The first structure was a simple hut of stone and timber—Geralt and Mika's."
  - line: 91
    type: narration
    text: "The second was a long barracks for the soldiers."
  - line: 92
    type: narration
    text: "It was basic, drafty, and home."
  - line: 94
    type: narration
    text: "Month 2 brought order."
  - line: 95
    type: narration
    text: "Merra Sundrift arrived from Ironspire with a caravan of seeds, tools, and stubborn hope."
  - line: 96
    type: narration
    text: "She walked the south-facing slope with Mika, pointing where the sun would linger."
  - line: 97
    type: narration
    text: "They planted the first fields."
  - line: 98
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt and the veterans channeled the stream, creating irrigation ditches with precise, military efficiency."
  - line: 99
    type: narration
    text: "A storage cache was dug into a cool hillside."
  - line: 101
    type: narration
    text: "Month 3 saw the valley become a settlement."
  - line: 102
    type: narration
    text: "More veterans arrived from Ironspire, their war ended, seeking the quiet company of their commanders."
  - line: 103
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck took charge of construction, his methodical, powerful presence perfect for lifting stone beams and plotting defensive lines."
  - line: 104
    type: narration
    text: "A low perimeter wall began to snake around the valley's most accessible approaches."
  - line: 106
    type: narration
    text: "The valley's strategic perfection was undeniable."
  - line: 107
    type: narration
    text: "It overlooked the only easy approach."
  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "The Star Needle Spire was a clear silhouette on the western horizon, a constant and comforting landmark."
  - line: 109
    type: narration
    text: "They had a two-mile sightline—any approaching threat would be seen with hours of warning."
  - line: 111
    type: narration
    text: "One morning, as Mika inspected the growing wall, she turned and found Zephyr standing beside her, as if he'd been there for hours."
  - line: 112
    type: narration
    text: "He was studying the masonry."
  - line: 114
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Perimeter's good,\""
  - line: 115
    type: narration
    text: "the ancient Sage said, not looking at her. \"Won't stop me, though.\""
  - line: 117
    type: narration
    text: "Then he was gone, leaving only the scent of ozone and timelessness."
  - line: 119
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 4: THE FIRST TONGUE"
  - line: 121
    type: narration
    text: "A year had gentled Falcon Ridge."
  - line: 122
    type: narration
    text: "The fields were green."
  - line: 123
    type: narration
    text: "The huts had become houses."
  - line: 124
    type: narration
    text: "The archive was Mika's pride—a solid stone building with a vaulted ceiling, filled with empty shelves waiting for knowledge."
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "One evening, Geralt, Mika, and Zephyr sat by the central fire."
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "The conversation drifted, as it often did with Zephyr, toward the deep past."
  - line: 129
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Zephyr
    text: "\"The First Tongue isn't spoken,\""
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "Mika leaned forward."
  - line: 132
    type: narration
    text: "\"The language of creation?\""
  - line: 134
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"One of them. The one this world was sung in.\""
  - line: 135
    type: narration
    text: "He looked at her, his ancient eyes reflecting the fire. \"Would you like to hear a word?\""
  - line: 137
    type: narration
    text: "She nodded."
  - line: 139
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Zephyr
    text: "\"Sek'han,\""
  - line: 141
    type: narration
    text: "Mika looked at a fist-sized stone near her foot."
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "She focused, not on moving it with force, but on introducing the concept of sek'han to it."
  - line: 143
    type: narration
    text: "She didn't speak aloud."
  - line: 144
    type: narration
    text: "She let the meaning form in her mind, in her will."

=inferred:
  emotions:
    - {line: 95, subject: Month, emotion: hope, confidence: 0.90}
  actions:
    - {line: 16, action: speak, confidence: 0.90}
    - {line: 115, action: speak, confidence: 0.90}

